note top of ArchiveModel
  BAD DESIGNS:
  • God object — archive + NFS + UI state in one class
  • listChildren() branches on isNfsMounted() instead of polymorphism
  • Legacy NfsIO path still embedded
end note

note top of ArchiveController
  BAD DESIGNS:
  • currentNfsConfig duplicates model's mount state
  • isNfsMounted() originally checked only currentNfsConfig (fixed)
  • Large controller — mixes archive + NFS + file ops
end note

note top of FileSystemFactory
  BAD DESIGNS:
  • registerDefaults() hardcodes 3 drivers
  • Adding a new driver requires editing factory (OCP violation)
end note

note top of NfsSftpFsIO
  BAD DESIGNS:
  • withChannel() opens a new SSH session per operation
  • listDirectory() makes 2 separate channel calls
  • No connection pooling
end note

@enduml
